    <statement><p>Determine whether the series converges, and if so find its sum.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{4^{k+4}}{7^{k}} =</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(Enter DNE if the sum does not exist.)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{7\cdot 4^{4+1}}{7^{0+1}\mathopen{}\left(7-4\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>a={\frac{1024}{7}}</m> and <m>r={\frac{4}{7}}</m>, <m>|r|\lt 1</m> so 


<m>\displaystyle \sum_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{4^{k+4}}{7^{k}} ={\frac{1024}{7}} \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} \left({\frac{4}{7}}\right)^{k} =\frac{{\frac{1024}{7}}}{1-\left({\frac{4}{7}}\right)}={\frac{1024}{3}}</m>


</solution>
